{192}{}{The Medical Facility, situated between the North and South Gates of the Rim, is overseen by the Followers of the Apocalypse. Whether you need patching up or seeking medicinal supplies, it's a valuable resource.}
{193}{}{Moving on, there's Downtown Engineering just to the west. While it may not seem like much, paying them a visit could prove enlightening. Plus, the entrance to the Baseline lies nearby.}
{194}{}{Speaking of which, the Baseline houses the only two functioning power generators in Hoover Dam, along with a group of reclusive individuals we affectionately refer to as "trogs" - short for troglodytes. They tend to keep to themselves in the dim, musty corridors.}
{195}{}{You'll find the Council Hall beyond the North Gate. It serves as the epicenter of administration, government, and military leadership.}
{196}{}{Venturing southwest of Downtown, you'll stumble upon the agricultural area. Here, Dave and his crew toil tirelessly to stave off hunger - a noble yet unglamorous task.}
{197}{}{Nearby, the NCR Army has established barracks, a testament to their ongoing conflicts driven by the politics of expansionism. While I avoid such places, I occasionally find myself there for boxing sponsorship matches.}
{198}{}{For those seeking adventure, "Hock-it to Bob" offers bounty hunting opportunities, while caravan companies on the Rim are perpetually on the lookout for intrepid travelers.}
{199}{}{Lastly, don't forget to pay a visit to Otto, the ghoul mechanic at Downtown Engineering. He's a master of his craft and might just have some special weaponry up his sleeve - assuming he's not indulging in a siesta.}
